Mango ships with other people's work.

Suwayomi-Server
  The extension host's `runtime.jar` (`host/runtime.jar` in a release archive,
  `/opt/mango/host/runtime.jar` in the Docker image) is Suwayomi-Server's release
  jar with files removed and nothing else changed. Suwayomi-Server is licensed
  under the Mozilla Public License 2.0. Its source is at
  https://github.com/Suwayomi/Suwayomi-Server, at the version Mango's `Dockerfile`
  names as SUWAYOMI_VERSION; the same file lists what was removed. The jar carries
  further libraries, each under its own licence.

Bouncy Castle
  The extension host's `bcprov.jar`, beside `runtime.jar`, is the Legion of the
  Bouncy Castle's signed provider jar, unchanged, at the version Mango's
  `Dockerfile` names as BCPROV_VERSION. It is under the MIT licence; the text is
  inside the jar at META-INF/LICENSE.md.

The programs and the web UI
  `mango` and `mango-desktop` are built from Rust crates, and the web UI inside
  `mango` carries Svelte and the two fonts below. The licence of each is in
  THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt: beside this file in a release archive, in
  `/usr/share/doc/mango` in the Docker image, and built from a checkout by
  `docker buildx build --target notices -o out .`

In the Docker image only
  A Java runtime linked from Eclipse Temurin (OpenJDK, GPL-2.0 with the Classpath
  Exception), Debian's base system, and the DejaVu fonts.

Fonts in the web UI
  Dela Gothic One and Zen Kaku Gothic New, both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
